"""
Ideal per-circuit ABS modulator: the ECU commands the wheel-side pressure it allows, and the valve
makes the caliper follow it after the solenoid lag `T_v`, never above the master-cylinder
pressure.

Ports: `port_a` the master-cylinder side; `port_b` the brake-line and caliper side; `p_cmd` the
allowed wheel-circuit pressure, gauge.

With p_a and p_b the two sides' gauge pressures:

- a command at or above p_a leaves the inlet open: p_b = p_a, and the fluid passes straight
  through;
- below p_a the valve holds or dumps: the held pressure p_hold relaxes to the command, clamped to
  [0, p_a], with the time constant `T_v`, and p_b = min(p_a, max(p_hold, 0)). While the inlet is
  open, p_hold follows p_a with the time constant `T_open`, so a closing valve starts from the
  pressure it held.

`return_dump` decides where fluid dumped from the caliper goes. At 0 it leaves the model, so the
master cylinder makes up every dumped volume and the pedal creeps forward without pulsing. At 1 it
re-enters at `port_a`, as if an ideal return pump with no accumulator pushed it straight back to
the master cylinder: the pedal is pushed back with every dump, the pulsation a driver feels.
`m_dump` is the fluid that leaves the model.

Pressures are gauge: the ports carry absolute pressure, `p_amb` + p, as `Caliper` and
`MasterCylinder` read it.

Assumptions: the valve has no flow restriction and no volume of its own; the held pressure starts
at 0. `p_amb` defaults to 100325 Pa, the reference pressure of `VehicleComponents.DOT4`. `T_v`
lumps the electronics' and the solenoid's reaction (assumed).
"""
component ABSValve
  "Master-cylinder side"
  port_a = HydraulicComponents.Interfaces.Port() {^port_a}
  "Brake-line and caliper side"
  port_b = HydraulicComponents.Interfaces.Port() {^port_b}
  "Allowed wheel-circuit pressure, gauge; at or above the master-cylinder side the inlet is open"
  p_cmd = RealInput() {^p_cmd}
  "Electronics and solenoid reaction time"
  parameter T_v::Time(min = eps(Float64)) = 0.03
  "Time constant with which the held pressure follows the master cylinder while the inlet is open"
  parameter T_open::Time(min = eps(Float64)) = 1e-3
  "Dumped fluid: 0 leaves the model, 1 returns to the master-cylinder side"
  parameter return_dump::Real = 0.0
  "Ambient pressure, which a released circuit sits at"
  parameter p_amb::Pressure = 100325.0
  "Master-cylinder side pressure, gauge"
  variable p_a::Pressure
  "Wheel side pressure, gauge"
  variable p_b::Pressure
  "Pressure the closed valve holds the wheel side at, gauge"
  variable p_hold::Pressure = initial 0.0
  "Command clamped to the master-cylinder side"
  variable p_target::Pressure
  "Mass flow of dumped fluid leaving the model"
  variable m_dump::MassFlowRate
relations
  continuity(port_a.medium, port_b.medium)
  port_a.p = p_amb + p_a
  port_b.p = p_amb + p_b
  p_target = min(max(p_cmd, 0.0), max(p_a, 0.0))
  der(p_hold) = ifelse(p_cmd >= p_a, (p_a - p_hold) / T_open, (p_target - p_hold) / T_v)
  p_b = ifelse(p_cmd >= p_a, p_a, min(p_a, max(p_hold, 0.0)))
  port_a.m_flow = ifelse(p_cmd >= p_a, -port_b.m_flow, max(-port_b.m_flow, 0.0) - return_dump * max(port_b.m_flow, 0.0))
  m_dump = port_a.m_flow + port_b.m_flow
metadata {
  "Dyad": {"icons": {"default": "dyad://VehicleComponents/Chassis/Brakes/ABSValve.svg"}},
  "_links": {
    "port_a": {
      "Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"iconName": "hydraulic_port_a", "x1": -50, "x2": 50, "y1": 450, "y2": 550}}}
    },
    "port_b": {
      "Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"iconName": "hydraulic_port_b", "x1": 950, "x2": 1050, "y1": 450, "y2": 550}}}
    },
    "p_cmd": {
      "Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"x1": 450, "x2": 550, "y1": 950, "y2": 1050, "rot": 270}}}
    }
  }
}
end
